1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,300
I just rewatched Save the Last Dance, and this movie needs to be studied.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,980
Sarah is a dancer in high school, and her mom dies in a car accident on the same day as her failed Juilliard audition.

3
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:15,700
So she quits dance, moves to the south side of Chicago to live with her estranged father, and go to an all-black high school.

4
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:19,560
And she's got like three months left of her high school career, so it doesn't make any sense.

5
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:23,780
Shanil sees Sarah at the first day of school, and she's like, oh my god, this white girl is not going to survive.

6
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:25,640
Sarah's like, oh my god, what is that?

7
00:00:28,230 --> 00:00:30,210
Hip-hop? You don't say.

8
00:00:30,210 --> 00:00:35,550
In gym class, Sarah shows off her dancing skills on the balance beam that every inner-city school has.

9
00:00:35,710 --> 00:00:37,470
So Shanil's like, where'd you get those moves?

10
00:00:37,830 --> 00:00:40,670
And Sarah's like, I used to be a dancer, not a big deal.

11
00:00:40,750 --> 00:00:45,470
So Shanil invites her to Steps, an invite-only nightclub for serious dancers.

12
00:00:45,870 --> 00:00:52,450
Also coming to Steps is Shanil's brother, Derek, who tells Sarah that she better be prepared for some, like, hardcore dancing.

13
00:00:52,630 --> 00:00:54,010
This is the dancing at the club.

14
00:00:57,260 --> 00:01:01,200
This is the members-only, invite-only dance club.

15
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:04,600
Like, you have to be a serious dancer for this.

16
00:01:04,780 --> 00:01:06,600
You have to be a jabberwocky to be here, okay?

17
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:10,660
Derek starts dancing with Sarah, who's very white, and everybody knows it.

18
00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:18,860
It was at this point where I was like, okay, who actually wrote this?

19
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:19,600
This man.

20
00:01:20,160 --> 00:01:21,040
This is the guy.

21
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:22,640
And now it all makes sense.

22
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:27,380
Then Derek gives Sarah hip-hop lessons, which include learning how to crip-walk and sitting in a chair.

23
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:30,860
Then Sarah does one of these, and he's like, where'd you learn how to do that?

24
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:32,520
She's like, I used to be a dancer.

25
00:01:32,620 --> 00:01:33,460
I don't want to talk about it.

26
00:01:33,540 --> 00:01:36,420
She spends this whole movie begging for people to ask her about dance.

27
00:01:36,660 --> 00:01:40,780
Derek convinces her to dance again and audition for Juilliard again, and he is going to help with the hip-hop.

28
00:01:43,930 --> 00:01:44,790
I don't know.

29
00:01:45,470 --> 00:01:46,530
Maybe don't audition.

30
00:01:47,010 --> 00:01:49,030
Then she returns to the club.

31
00:01:49,090 --> 00:01:49,750
I can't.

32
00:01:49,950 --> 00:01:52,230
She returns back to the club, blacker than ever.

33
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:54,490
Look at her go.

34
00:01:55,770 --> 00:01:57,290
They're chanting their names.

35
00:01:57,290 --> 00:02:02,570
Sarah auditions for Juilliard, and she falls again and has to start over.

36
00:02:02,670 --> 00:02:06,210
But Derek, who has been watching from the back of the auditorium, is like, not my baby girl.

37
00:02:06,310 --> 00:02:08,990
So he runs up on stage and tells her he believes in her.

38
00:02:09,070 --> 00:02:13,050
Then she does hip-hop for Juilliard.

39
00:02:13,610 --> 00:02:18,380
I bet they've never seen that before.

40
00:02:21,070 --> 00:02:22,250
They are so impressed.

41
00:02:22,510 --> 00:02:23,870
They're like, she is so urban.

42
00:02:24,410 --> 00:02:25,750
She's like, wait till you see what I do with the chair.

43
00:02:27,270 --> 00:02:28,630
You didn't see that coming, did you?

44
00:02:28,770 --> 00:02:30,430
They're like, oh, that girl is good.

45
00:02:30,930 --> 00:02:31,990
Look at those gang signs.

46
00:02:31,990 --> 00:02:33,330
Welcome to Juilliard.

47
00:02:33,710 --> 00:02:35,570
Immediately admits her to Juilliard.

48
00:02:36,010 --> 00:02:37,770
He's like, I know talent when I see it.

49
00:02:38,210 --> 00:02:39,930
And it fulfills our diversity quota.

